# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-11-08 stream, 43.9 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on 8e83fcc, the third stream through
# the second capture card, its display at 60.000199 Hz. It is the fixture where the two arms of
# the replay part: the plain arm's worst blend run is 15 presents, and the dejitter arm, which is
# how the stream ran, makes one of 44, as the field did. That run starts at 862.58 s: a lock
# release of 0.65 s that only the dejitter arm makes, 1.5 s after a 126 ms hitch, every present
# about half way between two frames and all 44 drawn by the flow warp. The game hitched (20 to
# 100 ms) 129 times (176 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 19 times (26 an hour), in 53
# bursts, 14 of them with a stall; the longest stalls are 514 ms at about 2271 s and 472 ms at
# about 1750 s. No periodic stretch. The lock released 6 times. Of the 43 moves on the replay,
# 7 of them late, 5 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 45.247 s, from the 2721
# marked frames in its first 45 s, 2720 of them on time within 0.44 ms of that offset (p90).
# The video has no holes and opens on gameplay; the pause menu opens at video time 43:51.75, so
# the cut is 45.2 s to 2677.0 s. The log runs on past it into a second stream made on the same
# launch, which is not part of this fixture. Inside the cut, 8 seconds in 8 runs fall out of
# the 60 fps regime, each a single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships with the step tolerance off, as it was
# then. The replay line is the plain arm and reads synth 0.5% against 0.5%, runs >= 50 0
# against 0, pull wraps 34 against 33, and worst run 15 against the field's 44: the field ran
# dejitter, so that line is not the one to hold against it. On the dejitter arm blends are 763
# against 763, repeats 174 against 174, skips 47 against 47, pull wraps 33 against 33 and the
# worst run 44 against 44, hence max_worst_run_dejit 44 beside the plain arm's 15. The replay
# makes 43 moves and the field's log has 43 in the window. The field's 6 releases and the
# replay's 6 pair up, each within 0.48 ms.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
